---
import { agencyBenchmarks } from '../lib/agency-benchmarks';
import { services } from '../lib/service-catalog';
import { href } from '../lib/site';
const examples = ['social-posts', 'google-ads', 'homepage'].map((slug) => ({
  benchmark: agencyBenchmarks.find((item) => item.slug === slug)!,
  service: services.find((item) => item.slug === slug)!,
}));
---

<section class="section cream-section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>A little price<br />perspective.</h2><p>
        A few estimated agency costs beside our fees, with the scope assumptions kept in view.
      </p>
    </div><div class="comparison-grid">
      {
        examples.map(({ benchmark, service }) => (
          <article class="comparison-card">
            <>
              <p class="eyebrow">Other Agencies</p>
              <h3>{service.shortTitle}</h3>
              <p class="comparison-price">
                {benchmark.price} {benchmark.period}
              </p>
              <p>{benchmark.tooltipSummary}</p>
              <hr />
              <p>
                <strong>Force Multiplier: $400 {benchmark.fmPeriod}</strong>
              </p>
              <p>{service.deliverables[0]}</p>
              <a href={href(`/services/${service.slug}`)} class="text-link">
                Review FM’s service →
              </a>
            </>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div><p class="comparison-note">
      Agency estimates combine published pricing with scope-based effort assumptions; they are not
      quotes or guaranteed savings. Every FM service has a separate agreement, with third-party
      costs additional where needed. <a href={`${href('/services')}#price-comparison`}
        >See all service comparisons.</a
      >
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
